			"date": "2024-07-22T23:18:02.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I keep wanting a \"filter to maintainer comments\" option. It's so easy to find a high traffic issue and have the most important comments get buried under tons of noise.</p><p>I want to answer questions like \"Is this going to be fixed, or is the maintainer pushing back for whatever reason?\" \"Is there a workaround?\" \"Is there a suggested alternative?\" The maintainer will answer those questions, everything else tends to be garbage.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
